+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+In confirmed MAIN standby, a fresh gas press of at least 0.1s and release requests SET−/release/SET−/release regardless of engagement or lateral activity. The second press continues after first engagement and can lower set speed by one step. Brake, CANCEL, MAIN OFF, renewed gas, driver buttons, lost eligibility or cancellation stop the remainder. Cancellation takes priority; normal speed buttons resume after the pair.
+
+Automatic SET uses only a newly observed CLU11 sample received within 8ms. Do not add a 10ms delay or remember a timing slot. Skip older samples and await the next within the original pedal/press deadlines, without extending their expiry.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+While parked, update both host and Panda and restart with MAIN OFF, then press MAIN ON after boot. Initial MAIN OFF is independent of AutoEngage. One release permits at most one pair; another requires three seconds after the last TX and a fresh pedal cycle. Blocked/expired cues are not queued. Option OFF revokes permission while preserving MAIN tracking.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Each press is at most three frames/60ms, separated by about 80ms, completing in about 0.2s. Panda checks six frames total, at least 60ms release separation and a 240ms envelope. Retain 0.5s MAIN settling, initial target/dashboard 30–160km/h and existing input/driver-priority guards. The current double-SET profile also requires front-left and rear-right wheel speeds at 30–160km/h. Discard releases below that wheel floor even if the dashboard exceeds 30; a fresh pedal cycle is required after speed recovers. `sample_age_ms` and `late_samples` report sample age and late-sample count. Absolute MAIN state is not decoded; standby already ON at restart needs a MAIN-OFF restart or actual stock ON from physical SET for synchronization. TX echo is not ECU acceptance; no direct braking, standstill launch or vehicle acceptance guarantee is provided.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
